[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The stew is presented in two simple, wide-rimmed matte ceramic bowls, centered on the surface to ensure full visibility of the contents for a 3/4 overhead perspective at 40 degrees. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, with the second bowl softly blurred behind it to represent two servings. The stew features a vibrant, thick base of softened diced bell peppers and onions, with hearty brown rice and quinoa grains visibly hydrated by the rich, amber-hued tomato and vegetable broth. Plump, opaque pink shrimp are nestled amongst the grains and vegetables, not stacked, ensuring each component is distinct and recognizable. A generous scattering of bright green chopped fresh parsley adds a pop of color. Shallow depth of field, with soft natural light streaming from the left, highlighting the slight sheen of extra-virgin olive oil on the surface of the stew and the soft texture of the cooked tomatoes. The setting is a rustic, aged oak tabletop with visible wood grain. Props include a tarnished silver fork resting casually beside the front bowl, a slightly rumpled linen napkin underneath the bowl, and a few stray grains of brown rice and a single green parsley leaf scattered near the rim. A small, blurred ramekin of extra sherry vinegar sits in the background. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures the warmth of a home-cooked meal, with slight natural imperfections: a tiny, realistic splash of red broth on the bowl's rim and an asymmetric distribution of ingredients. Warm, golden-hour lighting. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no text, no watermarks, no hands."
]
